The adapted portions are platform type declarations, the platform-interface
adapter and validation stub, TUN options and route-prefix iterators, default
interface monitoring, platform DNS transport, Android procfs connection-owner
lookup, Unix interface flags, descriptor duplication and Darwin utun lookup.
These remain licensed under GNU GPL version 3 or any later version, without
warranty; see the repository LICENSE and https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html.
The upstream utun descriptor lookup credits WireGuard/wireguard-apple.

This is an independently maintained compatibility surface, not the complete
upstream mobile SDK. CommandServer is only an in-process lifecycle wrapper.
No RPC listener, profile editor, SSH helper implementation, schema export,
management controller, OOM recorder, or configuration snapshot is included.

The build overlays these Go files into the pinned source module and generates
registry_selected.go. It must define baseContext(PlatformInterface)
context.Context, using only selected registries and filemanager.WithDefault
with sWorkingPath, sTempPath, sUserID and sGroupID. A selected local DNS transport
may call newPlatformTransport. The generated selectedFeaturesJSON constant
contains the canonical effective selection and gates shared TLS/transport code
at runtime, in addition to the exact typed protocol registries.
CoreFingerprint is supplied with linker -X
for github.com/sagernet/sing-box/experimental/libbox.coreFingerprint.

Default engine logging is suppressed. Explicitly requested log files are private
and receive fixed lifecycle events, never raw protocol diagnostics or auth URLs.
Platform and handler binding types for unsupported host features remain for
source compatibility; their core implementations return an unsupported error.
